# The vendored devbin runtime is not this project's to format (Devbin issue
# 0008): a formatting hook that rewrites bin/.devbin/lib/ does so inside an
# install/upgrade commit and breaks the vendored manifest one doctor later.
#
# This project's hook is the raw-prettier shape rather than the fleet's, so the
# fence was proven here before the install: without it a probe .md under
# bin/.devbin/lib/ came back rewritten; with it, byte-identical, while a project
# .md staged alongside was still formatted normally.
bin/.devbin/lib/

# Generated views have ONE writer, and it is the renderer (hv, 2026-08-19,
# ST0056 AC-03.17 in Intent's own tree). The hook above is the same one that
# made the devbin fence necessary -- a raw `prettier --write` over staged .md
# with a `git add` of its own rewrite -- so it is a second writer of every
# generated view here too.
#
# MEASURED HERE, 2026-08-26: NO SKEW TODAY -- `intent doctor` is 0 findings
# over 17 views and prettier reproduces every tracked view byte-for-byte. This
# is preventive. The failure it prevents is not a bad render but an unfixable
# one: once the two writers disagree, `sync --to-disk` repairs the file and the
# next commit undoes the repair, so `doctor` reports the skew for ever.
#
# Only renderer-owned paths are listed. design.md / impl.md / tasks.md /
# intent/wip.md / intent/done.md are authored, stay formatted, and are
# deliberately absent -- verified against the renderer in a sibling v3 repo by
# perturb-and-resync, not assumed from the directory they sit in.
#
# `**` rather than `*`: .prettierignore takes gitignore semantics, where a
# single `*` stops at a `/`.
intent/st/**/info.md
intent/st/**/acceptance.md
intent/st/steel_threads.md
intent/todo.md
